# The artist's own files are hashed by `tests/test_appicon.py`, which is how we
# know nobody has quietly edited a delivery.  Git for Windows checks out with
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this line it rewrites every LF in an `.svg`
# to CRLF on the way out of the object store, the file on disk is no longer the
# file the artist sent, and both hash tests fail on the two Windows CI jobs and
# on neither Linux one.  Marking SVG as not-text turns the conversion off while
# still letting `git diff` show it as text.
*.svg -text
